\section{Introduction}
\subsection{Purpose}
\label{sec:introduction:purpose}
This Software Requirements Specification (SRS) document outlines the requirements for a simple task management web application. This application aims to help users organize and track their tasks effectively.

\subsection{Scope}
\label{sec:introduction:scope}
The scope of this project is to develop a web application that allows users to create, view, update, and delete tasks. It will also include the ability to mark tasks as complete. This initial version will focus on core task management functionalities and will be accessible through a web browser.

\subsection{Intended Audience}
\label{sec:introduction:audience}
This document is intended for the following stakeholders:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Developers who will build the application.
    \item Testers who will verify the functionality and quality of the application.
    \item Project Managers who will oversee the development process.
    \item End-users who will use the task management application.
\end{itemize}

