\section{Overall Description}
\subsection{Product Perspective}
\label{sec:overall:perspective}
The Simple Task Management Web App will be a standalone, web-based application accessible through standard web browsers. It will not initially integrate with other external systems. The application will manage task data within its own persistent storage.

\subsection{Product Functions}
\label{sec:overall:functions}
The application will provide the following core functions:
\begin{itemize}
    \item **Task Creation:** Allow users to add new tasks with a title and optional description.
    \item **Task Viewing:** Allow users to view a list of their active and completed tasks.
    \item **Task Updating:** Allow users to edit the title and description of existing tasks.
    \item **Task Deletion:** Allow users to remove tasks.
    \item **Task Completion:** Allow users to mark tasks as complete and view their completed tasks.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{User Characteristics}
\label{sec:overall:characteristics}
The intended users are individuals who need a simple way to manage their personal or professional tasks. They are expected to have basic computer literacy and familiarity with web browsers. No specialized technical skills are required.

\subsection{Constraints}
\label{sec:overall:constraints}
\begin{itemize}
    \item **Technology:** The application should be developed using common web technologies (e.g., HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and a suitable backend framework and database). \textit{[We can specify these further if needed.]}
    \item **Simplicity:** The application should maintain a simple and intuitive user interface.
    \item **Time:** The development should be completed within a reasonable timeframe. \textit{[Specific timeframe to be determined.]}
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Assumptions and Dependencies}
\label{sec:overall:assumptions}
\begin{itemize}
    \item It is assumed that users will have access to a modern web browser and an internet connection.
    \item It is assumed that basic security measures will be implemented to protect user data.
\end{itemize}

\section{Specific Requirements}
\subsection{Functional Requirements}
\label{sec:specific:functional}
\subsubsection{FR1: Create Task}
\label{sec:specific:functional:1}
\textbf{Description:} The system shall allow users to create a new task with a title (mandatory) and an optional description.
\textbf{Input:} Task title (text input), optional task description (text area).
\textbf{Processing:} Upon submission, the system shall store the new task with a unique identifier, the provided title, description, and an initial status of "incomplete". The creation timestamp should also be recorded.
\textbf{Output:} Successful creation message to the user. The new task should be visible in the active task list.

\subsubsection{FR2: View Active Tasks}
\label{sec:specific:functional:2}
\textbf{Description:} The system shall display a list of all tasks that are currently marked as "incomplete". The tasks should be presented with their titles.
\textbf{Input:} User request to view active tasks.
\textbf{Processing:} The system shall retrieve all tasks with the status "incomplete" from the database.
\textbf{Output:} A list of active tasks, displaying at least the title of each task.

\subsubsection{FR3: View Completed Tasks}
\label{sec:specific:functional:3}
\textbf{Description:} The system shall allow users to view a list of all tasks that have been marked as "complete". The tasks should be presented with their titles and completion date/time.
\textbf{Input:} User request to view completed tasks.
\textbf{Processing:} The system shall retrieve all tasks with the status "complete" from the database.
\textbf{Output:} A list of completed tasks, displaying at least the title and completion date/time of each task.

\subsubsection{FR4: Update Task}
\label{sec:specific:functional:4}
\textbf{Description:} The system shall allow users to edit the title and description of an existing incomplete task.
\textbf{Input:} Selection of a task from the active task list, modified task title (text input), and/or modified task description (text area).
\textbf{Processing:} Upon submission, the system shall update the title and/or description of the selected task in the database. The update timestamp should also be recorded.
\textbf{Output:} Successful update message to the user. The updated task should be reflected in the active task list.

\subsubsection{FR5: Delete Task}
\label{sec:specific:functional:5}
\textbf{Description:} The system shall allow users to delete an existing incomplete task.
\textbf{Input:} Selection of a task from the active task list and confirmation of deletion.
\textbf{Processing:} Upon confirmation, the system shall remove the selected task from the database.
\textbf{Output:} Successful deletion message to the user. The deleted task should no longer be visible in the active task list.

\subsubsection{FR6: Mark Task as Complete}
\label{sec:specific:functional:6}
\textbf{Description:} The system shall allow users to mark an incomplete task as "complete".
\textbf{Input:} Selection of a task from the active task list.
\textbf{Processing:} Upon selection, the system shall update the status of the selected task to "complete" and record the completion timestamp in the database.
\textbf{Output:} The task should be moved from the active task list to the completed task list.

